{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Hey, slip in here a sec. I'll grab vitals, he's stuck on the computer again.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok. Um, my hands are kinda cold, sorry.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): You're good. 128 over 78, pulse 92, sat 99 percent, breathing 16, temp 36.8.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): 92. Is that bad? I don't know.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Not my call. Your partner phoned the desk though. Said you texted from the platform, chest locked up, you were shaking, they wanted it in the note.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): They weren't there. I was alone. The train was packed and then it just hit me.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ugh, sorry. Lost the screen. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): This morning on the train, uh, my chest got really tight out of nowhere, and I started shaking, and I got so scared I thought I was having a heart attack. I'm 24, that shouldn't even...",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Wait, say that again? I typed over it.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Tight chest. Shaking. Thought it was a heart attack. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): How long did the tightness last?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, maybe ten minutes. Err. It eased off after I got off the train.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): And the shaking, same time?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Hands, and kind of everywhere. That's done. I'm not shaking sitting here.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Still tight at all?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Gone. I'm just scared it's gonna come back.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't think so. I mean, no.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, repeat that, the vent is loud. Fever yes or no, and have you been coughing?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever. No cough.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): What about your weight, up or down?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. Maybe down a little. I don't weigh myself so I can't really say.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. Medicines?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Nothing prescribed right now. Well, actually, I take the little orange vitamin D gummies, one a day. And I've still got that blue inhaler from the bronchitis last winter, but I haven't used it in months.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Blue inhaler, say the name again, I was in the med list.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): I think the label says albuterall. It's just the blue puffer. I don't know, doctor. It sits in a drawer.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (NURSE): Partner also said on the phone, no drugs, no pills, nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. I don't smoke. A beer on the weekend, that's it. I was just heading to work, the bookstore on 4th.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Allergies? Meds, food, whatever.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): No. None.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ever had your heart checked? An old tracing?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Student health, like two years ago. They did an EKG and they said it was borderline. Didn't explain it. Sent me home.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Borderline. A number, a quote, anything?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. No number. Just that word, borderline.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ok. I was gonna say your lungs, but I haven't listened, ignore that. Looking at you, color's good, you're talking in full sentences, no distress.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): We'll do an ECG today, twelve lead, down the hall before you go. This sounds like a panic attack to me, a first one, not a heart attack, but I'm not skipping the tracing.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): If it starts on the train again, in through your nose, slow out through your mouth, longer on the way out. Come back in two weeks and we'll look at the ECG together. Crushing pain that won't let up, or you faint, you go to the ER, don't ride it out."
 ],
